        }
      ],
      "key": "calculus_layers",
      "label": "Calculus, interpreted model and encoded carrier"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Finite local derivation owners cover scoped identity/authority and bounded-context meaning in FOUNDATIONS §2; bounded probabilistic construction in P0, Work boundary and ACTIVATION §1; delegation/candidate production/independent assessment in ACTIVATION §1 and EVALUATION §3; ambiguity/human adjudication/hard stops in ACTIVATION §4; exact basis, authority, evidence/verdict separation and results in RF-005–007 and FOUNDATIONS; constitutional derivation/re-entry in SPEC_METHOD §§1,4; closure/projection/residual/capability law in REFERENCE_FRAME §3; singular release authority in SPEC_METHOD §6 and PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4. AxiomaticCalculusBasis resolves these to immutable absolute clause addresses in derivation_basis.principle_refs. Generic F_D, F_P and F_H originate here, independently of equal-spelled runtime/profile/application terms.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 63,
          "quote": "The calculus specialises the governing commitments declared in this\npackage. Its derivation basis is the following finite set of current local\nowners, resolved to exact clauses by the identity record of §8 (P6):",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FDerivation%20provenance",
          "start_line": 61
        }
      ],
      "key": "calculus_derivation_basis",
      "label": "Calculus derivation basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Material family F9's premise-to-rule account distinguishes derived consequences from owner-selected choices. Instance premises, not supplied by commitments, are: a finite model represents governed objects/relations/constraints/residuals/traversals/transformations/judgments; exact subject, interpreted model and possible carrier have separate identities; some predicates are mechanical and others need bounded probabilistic construction or explicit human adjudication. P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 are marked independent; P0 recovered; P4b derived from P0/P2; P5 derived from P0/P6. Nineteen rows bind these premises to position, scope, signature, identity/typing, authority/basis, results, latitude, residuals, closure/projection, overlay, transformation, judgment separation, traversal/composition, interpretation, layers, identity issuance, application/import boundaries, constraint surfaces and qualification.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 158,
          "quote": "This member is material family F9, the `a_c` calculus. The table below\nshows which of its rules follow from which premises, in the format of\n[FOUNDATIONS §3 Foundation to law](FOUNDATIONS.md#foundation-to-law),\nwhich also states the standing of the consequences. Instance premises,\nwhich the commitments do not supply:\n\n- (i) a governed symbolic system is represented by a finite model whose\n  records stand for its objects, relations, constraints, residuals,\n  traversals, transformations and judgments;\n- (ii) a model is interpreted from an exact subject and may be encoded in\n  a carrier, and subject, model and carrier are separately identified;\n- (iii) some predicates over a model are decided mechanically, and others\n  need bounded probabilistic construction or explicit human adjudication.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F1.%20Position%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line": 146
        }
      ],
      "key": "foundation_law_account",
      "label": "Foundation-to-law account"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Sigma = (RecordKind, Sort, RelationKind, ConstraintKind, ResidualKind, FunctorKind, JudgmentKind, StopKind). RecordKind_ac fixes eight urn:stdo:concept:axiomatic-calculus:record-kind: identities ending semantic-object, typed-relation, constraint, latitude, residual, traversal, transformation and judgment. Each signature member is a finite closed identity set for one model family. The signature specifies fields/value domains, reference domains/cardinalities, relation endpoint sorts, constraint subject/predicate domains, residual subject/uncertainty/consequence/re-entry domains, judgment input/output/evidence/stop contracts and permitted traversal functor kinds.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 228,
          "quote": "Sigma = (\n  RecordKind,\n  Sort,\n  RelationKind,\n  ConstraintKind,\n  ResidualKind,\n  FunctorKind,\n  JudgmentKind,\n  StopKind\n)",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature",
          "start_line": 219
        }
      ],
      "key": "subject_signature",
      "label": "Subject a_c signature"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "M_b = (b, I, O, E, C, L, X, V, T, J), with exact basis b, closed identity universe I and finite populations for semantic objects, directed relations, constraints, latitude, residuals, traversals, transformations and judgments. Population_M is total over the eight core kinds. Local_M is their disjoint union; I = Local_M disjoint_union External_M. RefDomain_Sigma(record_kind, field) yields cardinality, allowed local kinds, semantic-object sorts, external target kinds and required basis relation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 302,
          "quote": "`Population_M` is a total function over `RecordKind_ac`. Every population\nis finite, every fundamental record belongs to exactly one population, and\nrecord identities are unique across their disjoint union. Let `Local_M` be\nthat union. Then `I = Local_M disjoint_union External_M`, where every\nmember of `External_M` is admitted only through one signature-declared\nexternal reference domain and exact resolution relation. A hidden record,\nan unpopulated extra record family, an identity occurring in two\npopulations, or an identity in `I` with neither one local record nor one\nlawful external resolution refuses the model. A population may be empty\nonly when the selected signature does not require a member of that record\nkind (P3, P5).",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-common/35fb4824a064a84df5af214a0d0e2da597c18ac6/source/standards/AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS.md#AXIOMATIC_CALCULUS%2F2.%20Signature",
          "start_line": 292
